/* book Worked example: Q: A single-phase bridge cycloconverter is fed from 230 V, 50 Hz and supplies a 10 Ω resistive load at one third of the supply frequency. Both groups are fired at α = 60° in every half cycle. Find the output frequency and period, the RMS output voltage and current, the load power and the input power factor.
   1. fo = 50/3 = 16.67 Hz, so To = 1/16.67 = 60 ms: the P group gives three positive humps (30 ms), then the N group three negative humps.
   2. Each hump is a half sine conducted from 60° to 180°, as in an AC voltage controller. α = π/3, sin 120° = 0.866: bracket = (π − π/3 + 0.433)/π = (2.094 + 0.433)/π = 0.8045.
   3. Vo = 230 × √0.8045 = 230 × 0.8969 = 206.3 V. Io = 206.3/10 = 20.63 A.
   4. P = 206.3²/10 = 4256 W. Input power factor = Vo/Vs = 206.3/230 = 0.897.
   Answer: fo = 16.67 Hz, To = 60 ms, Vo = 206.3 V, Io = 20.63 A, P = 4.26 kW, power factor 0.897. */
