/* book Worked example: Q: A 415 V, 50 Hz supply feeds a star-connected resistive load of 20 Ω per phase through a three-phase matrix converter with q = 0.5 and an output frequency of 30 Hz. Find the output phase voltage, the load current, the total power and the input line current, assuming no losses and unity input power factor. What is the largest power available from this load?
   1. Input phase voltage Vin = 415/√3 = 239.6 V.
   2. Vo = qVin = 0.5 × 239.6 = 119.8 V per phase; the 30 Hz is set by the modulation.
   3. Io = 119.8/20 = 5.99 A. P = 3 × 119.8²/20 = 2153 W.
   4. Input current from the power balance: P = √3 × 415 × Iin, so Iin = 2153/(1.732 × 415) = 3.00 A.
   5. Largest output: q = 0.866 gives Vo = 0.866 × 239.6 = 207.5 V, so Pmax = 3 × 207.5²/20 = 6.46 kW.
   Answer: Vo = 119.8 V, Io = 5.99 A, P = 2.15 kW, Iin = 3.00 A. q = 0.5 is inside the 0.866 limit; the most this load can take is 6.46 kW at 207.5 V per phase. */
